<title>SOUTH KOREA: S.Korea's KFA to seek 125,000 tonnes of soymeal.</title>
<headline>S.Korea's KFA to seek 125,000 tonnes of soymeal.</headline>
<dateline>SEOUL 1997-01-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>South Korea's Korea Feed Association (KFA) will invite tenders for 125,000 tonnes of soymeal by 2.00 p.m. (0500 GMT) on Monday, an official with the association said on Wednesday.  </p>
<p>The KFA official said the tenders were divided into four positions for arrival by March 20.</p>
<p>Shipment was set for March 1-20 if sourced from China, for February 14-March 5 if sourced from India, or for January 20-February 8 if from South America or the U.S. Gulf.</p>
<p>Details for the tenders are as follows:</p>
<p> POSITION  TONNE     ETA	   PORT</p>
<p>  ONE	50,000    March 20    Inchon/Ulsan/Kunsan</p>
<p>  TWO	35,000    March 20    Inchon/Ulsan/Kunsan</p>
<p>  THREE    20,000    March 20    Inchon</p>
<p>  FOUR     20,000    March 20    Ulsan/Kunsan</p>
<p>--Seoul Newsroom (822)727 5651</p>
</text>
